nodes.body:
@18930666888 Thanks for sharing this deployment case. Could you provide the full boot log, launch command, and exact SGLang revision, and clarify whether this PR was applied?
This patch removes unintended retention of loader-owned Parameters; it does not remove the memory required by MTP itself. Since the 81.8 GiB figure references the cookbook’s 96GB measurement, a same-configuration comparison with and without this patch would help establish the actual benefit on your card. The selected quantization/MoE backend and the stage where startup fails would also be useful.
@Qiaolin-Yu Could you please review this focused two-file fix and authorize CI with /tag-and-rerun-ci? The existing evidence includes CPU lifetime A/B tests and reporter validation on 2×L20/TP2, where the baseline OOMed at repack layer 9 and the fix completed all 48 layers and served requests. The visible Base CI run is still blocked at the run-ci label gate.
The additional SM120/MTP deployment impact is not yet A/B-validated; I’m following up on that separately from the already validated loader-lifetime fix. Thank you.

